Everyone seems to have their own speedpainting method. This is the method that I've found works for me best. It combines both speed while still looking decent, and layering techniques so it hides each individual method.

To find out how fast it was, I decided to time each step. This also lets you see what step had the biggest impact compared to the amount of time it takes.

For this, I am painting a Farrow force to be used for demo games for Warmachine. These models are STL's that are a part of the welcome pack of the [Warmachine MyMiniFactory|https://www.myminifactory.com/users/Warmachine].

A overview of the method is:
* Airbrush undertones
* Speedpaints
* Enamel Wash
* Quick Hightlights
* Effects

The total time is summarised in the table below. These models were done as a batch, the time taken is to complete that step on every model.

